.* DSPLOG: the history log's messages, oldest first.
:PNLGRP.
:COPYR.(C) Quartz Systems 2026
:CLASS NAME=LINECL BASETYPE='CHAR 77'.
:ECLASS.
:VAR NAME=LINE CLASS=LINECL.
:LISTDEF NAME=LOG VARS='LINE'.
:KEYL NAME=KEYS HELP=KEYSHLP.
:KEYI KEY=ENTER ACTION=ENTER.
:KEYI KEY=HELP ACTION='RETURN 1'.
:KEYI KEY=F1 ACTION='RETURN 1'.
:KEYI KEY=F3 ACTION=EXIT.F3=Exit
:KEYI KEY=F10 ACTION='RETURN 10'.F10=Display all
:KEYI KEY=F12 ACTION=CANCEL.F12=Cancel
:KEYI KEY=F17 ACTION=TOP.
:KEYI KEY=F18 ACTION=BOTTOM.
:KEYI KEY=PAGEUP ACTION=PAGEUP.
:KEYI KEY=PAGEDOWN ACTION=PAGEDOWN.
:EKEYL.
:PANEL NAME=DSPLOG KEYL=KEYS HELP=DSPLOGH ENTER='RETURN 0' TOPSEP=SPACE.Display History Log Contents
:LIST DEPTH='*' LISTDEF=LOG SCROLL=YES.
:LISTCOL VAR=LINE USAGE=OUTPUT.
:ELIST.
:BOTINST.Press Enter to continue.
:EPANEL.
:HELP NAME=DSPLOGH.Display History Log Contents - Help
:P.The messages the system kept in its history log, oldest first. F10
adds when each was sent, its identifier and the job that sent it.
Place the cursor on a message and press F1 to see all of it.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=KEYSHLP.Function keys - Help
:P.F3 leaves the display, F12 goes back one display.
:EHELP.
:EPNLGRP.
